# Live Draft surface gating (RFSN-030)

`DraftWarRoom` stays mounted across `/draft/live` ↔ `/draft/mock`.
`liveDraftActive` is **sticky** (toggle ON survives Mock navigation).

## Rule

Any Live Draft service (broadcast snapshot poller, ESPN/connected-league monitor, clock engines, booth audio, live sockets) must be gated by **`isLiveDraftSurfaceActive`** (or equivalent: `liveDraftActive && preferLiveDraft`), **never** by `liveDraftActive` alone.

```ts
// ❌ Wrong — leaks onto Mock when toggle stays ON
enabled = liveDraftActive

// ✅ Correct
enabled = isLiveDraftSurfaceActive({ liveDraftActive, preferLiveDraft })
// connected-league also requires source === "connected-league"
```

Helpers: `client/src/lib/liveDraftSurfaceActive.ts`
- `isLiveDraftSurfaceActive`
- `isConnectedLeagueLiveActive`

## Monitor effects

Do not put unstable callback/mutation object identity (`notifyMut`, etc.) in poll-loop `useEffect` deps. Hold them in a ref so lifecycle inputs (`enabled`/`canRun`, `draftId`, `pollMs`, …) control start/stop — not render identity churn.
